From 6f3fbd91bf5a5a3d29dc9949e4ab4dc9f145ca1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Andr=C3=A9=20Machado?= <machaddr@falanet.org>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 20:40:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: boe: fix PineTab-V wake timing and DE polarity
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The PineTab-V panel loses the bootloader image when Linux takes over even
though the DSI host and display controller complete their atomic enable
sequence.  Two details differ from the implementation which displays the
Pine64 logo in U-Boot.

U-Boot and StarFive's Jadard panel driver wait 120 ms after the final F3
initialization command before leaving sleep mode.  The generic BOE driver
currently sends the two commands back-to-back.  Add a descriptor delay so
only the PineTab-V sequence gains the missing wait.

The working U-Boot display-controller setup also leaves the DC8200 DE
polarity bit clear.  StarFive's vendor panel data described active-low DE,
but its display-controller driver did not consume that flag.  The upstream
Verisilicon bridge does consume it, producing the opposite electrical
polarity.  Describe PineTab-V's effective, known-working active-high DE
polarity explicitly.

These changes preserve the timings and signalling of the other panels
supported by this driver.

Link: https://github.com/starfive-tech/linux/blob/pinetabv-6.6.y-devel/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-starfive-jadard.c
Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5
Signed-off-by: André Machado <machaddr@falanet.org>
---
 .../drm/panel/panel-boe-th101mb31ig002-28a.c  | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-boe-th101mb31ig002-28a.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-boe-th101mb31ig002-28a.c
index 831f2c6fa..cbb69b78d 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-boe-th101mb31ig002-28a.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-boe-th101mb31ig002-28a.c
@@ -32,6 +32,7 @@ struct panel_desc {
 	unsigned int vcioo_to_lp11_delay_ms;
 	unsigned int lp11_to_reset_delay_ms;
 	unsigned int enable_to_reset_delay_ms;
+	unsigned int init_to_exit_sleep_delay_ms;
 	unsigned int backlight_off_to_display_off_delay_ms;
 	unsigned int enter_sleep_to_reset_down_delay_ms;
 	unsigned int power_off_delay_ms;
@@ -114,6 +115,9 @@ static int boe_th101mb31ig002_enable(struct boe_th101mb31ig002 *ctx)
 	mipi_dsi_dcs_write_seq_multi(&dsi_ctx, 0xf0, 0x12, 0x03, 0x20, 0x00, 0xff);
 	mipi_dsi_dcs_write_seq_multi(&dsi_ctx, 0xf3, 0x00);
 
+	if (ctx->desc->init_to_exit_sleep_delay_ms)
+		mipi_dsi_msleep(&dsi_ctx, ctx->desc->init_to_exit_sleep_delay_ms);
+
 	mipi_dsi_dcs_exit_sleep_mode_multi(&dsi_ctx);
 
 	mipi_dsi_msleep(&dsi_ctx, 120);
@@ -332,8 +336,9 @@ static const struct panel_desc pinetab_v_desc = {
 		      MIPI_DSI_MODE_VIDEO_SYNC_PULSE |
 		      MIPI_DSI_CLOCK_NON_CONTINUOUS |
 		      MIPI_DSI_MODE_LPM,
-	.bus_flags = DRM_BUS_FLAG_DE_LOW,
+	.bus_flags = DRM_BUS_FLAG_DE_HIGH,
 	.init = boe_th101mb31ig002_enable,
+	.init_to_exit_sleep_delay_ms = 120,
 	.enable_to_reset_delay_ms = 250,
 	.lp11_after_enable = true,
 	.lp11_to_reset_delay_ms = 5,
-- 
